WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.400
-Donald Trump took
the stand today

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.701
for an angry
and combative appearance

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:06.200
in his New York fraud trial,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.367
marking the first time
he's faced direct questioning

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:11.634
from prosecutors in court
as part of a sprawling case

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:13.434
that could wipe out
his entire business empire.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.868
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:19.567
♪♪

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.601
Just to recap,
throughout his presidency,

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:24.601
Donald Trump was consistently
the most disliked president

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:25.868
in the history of polling.

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:27.734
He lost the popular vote
by 3 million the first time

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.100
and 7 million the second time.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.300
He cost the GOP the House
in 2018 and the Senate in 2020.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.734
His hand-picked candidates
in 2022 were rejected

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.334
and humiliated in almost
every single race

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:37.567
where he played a major role.

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.667
He got impeached twice,
oversaw a disastrous

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:42.267
and incompetent response to a
once-in-a-generation pandemic.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:43.567
He orchestrated a coup attempt

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:45.601
and incited a riotous mob
to storm the Capitol

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:47.667
that threatened to kill
his own vice president

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:49.434
and install him
as an unelected dictator.

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:52.067
He's facing four separate
criminal cases,

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.501
as well as a civil fraud trial

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.167
that could erase
his entire business empire.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.367
And on top of all that,

00:00:56.367 --> 00:01:02.667
he's the weirdest human
being on the planet.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:05.234
So naturally, after all that,

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:08.601
he is finally slinking away
from the national spotlight

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.968
in disgrace to face consequences
for his behavior.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.334
And I'm just kidding.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:16.767
He's leading in the [bleep]
polls again by like a lot.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:18.067
-In the race
for the White House,

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:20.200
new polls are showing
some very unfavorable trends

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.534
for President Biden.

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:24.200
The latest CBS news poll
of likely voters

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.567
finds President Trump slightly
ahead of President Biden.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:30.701
-A "New York Times" poll of
six battleground states that

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:33.467
President Biden
won back in 2020.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:36.000
Now, in five out of six of those
states, Mr. Biden

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.868
is trailing Donald Trump.

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:40.200
He's behind by five in Arizona,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.667
six in Georgia and a startling
10 points in Nevada.

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:47.601
He's even trailing in states
like Michigan and Pennsylvania,

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:51.200
where the president has seen
strong Democratic support.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.000
-This brings us to
a new segment we're calling

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.634
"Seth Stares Off
Into The Distance

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.200
And Mutters To Himself
For A Second."

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.634
[ Muttering ]

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:10.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:15.300
[ Muttering ]

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:19.100
Biden's old,
but Trump's old, too.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:24.367
I mean, like...

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:25.567
Really...

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.200
I mean, some people say, "Oh,
this will be good for you,"

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.434
but get that out of your head.

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.067
This isn't a real cigarette.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:45.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been "Seth Stares Off
Into The Distance

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.601
And Mutters To Himself
For A Second."

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:53.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:57.234
Now, I know we are a full year
away from the election,

00:02:57.234 --> 00:02:58.734
and it's natural and normal
for people

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:00.067
to express
their frustration

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:01.801
with the incumbent
at this point in the calendar.

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.701
The same thing happened
with Obama too,

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:05.968
and then he went on
to easily defeat Mitt Romney.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.534
In fact, Gallup's final poll

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:08.868
before the election
had Romney ahead,

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:10.300
so there's no reason to panic.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.801
On the other hand, we have to
start [bleep] panicking now!

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:17.634
We are [bleep], [bleep],
[bleep], [bleep]!

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:20.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:25.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:31.167
-So, I guess this new poll
makes Trump the front runner,

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:33.968
not just for the GOP nomination,
but for the whole deal.

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:35.367
Yeah. I mean, okay, cool.

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.501
What a world.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:38.901
That would mean
the current front runner

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:40.767
to be the next president
spent the day in court

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:42.634
where he was grilled
on the stand by prosecutors

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:44.734
about his company's
alleged widespread fraud.

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:46.400
And this morning,
when he arrived in court,

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.567
he did his usual Trump shtick,

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.000
where he complained
about the proceedings

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.534
and lashed out
at everyone involved.

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:19.267
Maybe you should spend
less time coming up with names

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:22.601
for things and more time
coming up with a defense.

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:24.534
"Mr. President, we have
to explain to the judge

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.400
how you came up
with this net worth estimate."

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.267
"I call it warfare or lawfare.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.501
Or how about this one?
Law not fair.

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:33.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:35.734
I was up all night
for that one."

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.400
So far, the entirety
of the Trump defense

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.000
has basically been
that they had no idea

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.400
what was going on
at their own company.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.000
Last week, Trump's
two oldest sons,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.067
who were officers
at the company,

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:45.901
pleaded ignorance
when they took the stand.

00:04:45.901 --> 00:04:48.200
-Two of Trump's sons,
Don Jr., Eric as well,

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.033
who are
executive vice presidents

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.767
at the Trump Organization,
they both testified this week.

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:54.734
Both made arguments
that were nearly identical,

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:58.467
that it was the company's
accountants who,

00:04:58.467 --> 00:04:59.901
in fact, were responsible
for issues

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.367
with financial statements,
not them.

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:06.367
-I'm apparently guilty of fraud

00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:14.000
for relying on my accountants
to do, wait for it, accounting.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.334
I mean, think about that.

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:18.334
What does that do for literally
any other business?

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:21.834
You pay experts millions
of dollars to be experts.

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:24.334
You sign off
on what they give you.

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:27.033
-That's, wait for it,
not how it works.

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:28.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:31.200
By the way, I'd be fine if we
instituted automatic jail time

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.100
for anyone who does wait
for it in 2023.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.133
They're accountants.

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:36.300
You give them information,

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.934
and then they just
prepare the statements.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:39.667
They're not the ones
running your business.

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:41.334
You're supposed to be
in charge of them.

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:44.300
Also, you can't believably say
you employ experts

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.834
when your family
is also employed

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:49.267
the law firm of weirdo,
goofball and nuts.

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:52.534
Oh, no. Was Rudy Giuliani
also your accountant?

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:54.634
"Good news, boss,
I just did all the numbers,

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:56.267
and it's a unicorn.

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:58.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.467 --> 00:06:01.033
I was -- I'm as surprised
as you were, boss.

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:04.534
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.534 --> 00:06:06.901
It's a mythical creature.
Now we have proof."

00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:09.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:11.067
The other defense
they've been using before today

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:12.801
is that Trump's children
should be left alone,

00:06:12.801 --> 00:06:14.767
even though two of them
were officers of the company

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:17.434
who signed off
on the statements in question.

00:06:17.434 --> 00:06:19.501
-Trump is accusing
Attorney General James

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:21.601
of harassing him
and his children.

00:06:21.601 --> 00:06:23.467
-Mr. Trump
is lashing out online,

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:25.634
saying leave
my children alone.

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:28.734
-And now these children
are being brought in away

00:06:28.734 --> 00:06:31.901
from their families for
doing nothing wrong.

00:06:31.901 --> 00:06:36.267
-These poor innocent, lightly
bearded children

00:06:36.267 --> 00:06:37.734
are being brought in alone.

00:06:37.734 --> 00:06:41.100
Their nannies
have to wait outside,

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.801
which means they're going hours
between snacks.

00:06:43.801 --> 00:06:46.434
It is shameful.

00:06:46.434 --> 00:06:48.000
But today it was
Trump's turn to take the stand,

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.167
and let's just pause
for a moment

00:06:49.167 --> 00:06:50.501
to appreciate
how dramatic it is.

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:53.601
A former president being grilled
in court about systemic,

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:55.267
years long fraud at his company,

00:06:55.267 --> 00:06:57.634
which is the entire basis
of his fortune

00:06:57.634 --> 00:07:00.567
and his image as a supposedly
successful businessman.

00:07:00.567 --> 00:07:04.067
And this isn't even
one of the four criminal cases.

00:07:04.067 --> 00:07:05.400
This is just a civil case.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.601
We've become so inured
to Trump's flagrant

00:07:07.601 --> 00:07:08.934
lawbreaking and insanity

00:07:08.934 --> 00:07:10.767
that it barely registers
as news anymore.

00:07:10.767 --> 00:07:13.534
If Martin Van Buren
had been dragged into court

00:07:13.534 --> 00:07:14.901
on fraud allegations,

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:18.367
that would be the only thing
anyone remembers about it.

00:07:18.367 --> 00:07:20.334
Instead, all anyone
remembers about him

00:07:20.334 --> 00:07:23.834
is the "Seinfeld" episode.

00:07:23.834 --> 00:07:26.667
Or that's the only thing
Sal remembers about it.

00:07:26.667 --> 00:07:29.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.934 --> 00:07:33.300
And I'm sure it won't shock you
to learn that Trump was both

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.767
combative and uncooperative
during his testimony today.

00:07:35.767 --> 00:07:37.300
In fact, this morning
he couldn't even make it

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.901
through the first
half hour of testimony

00:07:38.901 --> 00:07:41.000
without repeatedly
picking fights with the judge

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.367
and getting yelled at.

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:44.167
-Happening now,
behind those doors,

00:07:44.167 --> 00:07:46.033
Donald Trump has been testifying

00:07:46.033 --> 00:07:48.067
in the civil fraud trial
against him.

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:51.667
He's been on the stand
for about 25 minutes or so.

00:07:51.667 --> 00:07:54.901
He has been admonished
by the judge.

00:07:54.901 --> 00:07:57.601
He has criticized the judge.

00:07:57.601 --> 00:07:59.267
The judge has told him to stick

00:07:59.267 --> 00:08:01.133
to answering
the questions in this,

00:08:01.133 --> 00:08:03.400
all within the first
minutes of testimony.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:04.567
-That's how it started.

00:08:04.567 --> 00:08:06.200
They couldn't even make it
25 minutes

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.901
without having to wrangle him
like they're trying

00:08:07.901 --> 00:08:09.033
to give medicine to a cat.

00:08:09.033 --> 00:08:12.033
He was supposedly
the Commander in Chief.

00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:13.667
He can't even get through
one day in court

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:15.334
without getting into
like nine different fights

00:08:15.334 --> 00:08:16.701
within the first 25 minutes.

00:08:16.701 --> 00:08:19.367
He's like a blue collar dad
at a fancy restaurant,

00:08:19.367 --> 00:08:23.501
immediately furious
he didn't get bread right away.

00:08:23.501 --> 00:08:27.734
"What kind of horse hockey
is this?

00:08:27.734 --> 00:08:30.968
I want butter, not a dish
full of chopped up olives.

00:08:30.968 --> 00:08:33.200
And why the hell
is everyone wearing a suit?

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.534
This is a restaurant,
not a funeral.

00:08:34.534 --> 00:08:35.868
Of course,
I wouldn't be surprised

00:08:35.868 --> 00:08:38.801
if someone dropped dead
when they saw these prices.

00:08:38.801 --> 00:08:42.767
Screw this,
I'm going to the Golden Corral."

00:08:42.767 --> 00:08:45.501
I told the valet guy just tell
me where you parked it."

00:08:45.501 --> 00:08:48.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:48.934 --> 00:08:50.601
In fact, things got so heated
that at one point

00:08:50.601 --> 00:08:51.934
the judge
had to turn away from Trump

00:08:51.934 --> 00:08:53.701
and appealed to his lawyers
to get him to behave.

00:08:53.701 --> 00:08:55.434
Now, because there are
no cameras inside,

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:56.934
we can't actually
see what happens,

00:08:56.934 --> 00:08:59.968
so we have to rely
on narration from reporters

00:08:59.968 --> 00:09:03.200
on even the smallest gestures
or facial expressions.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.634
-Let's get back out
to the courthouse.

00:09:04.634 --> 00:09:06.901
Paula Reid's got some
more detail from inside.

00:09:06.901 --> 00:09:10.300
What's happening?

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.100
-This is getting pretty heated.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:14.300
The judge asking
Trump's lawyer,

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.234
"Can you control your client?

00:09:16.234 --> 00:09:18.200
This is not a political rally."

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.767
This coming from our colleagues
who are inside

00:09:19.767 --> 00:09:22.334
the courtroom
watching this live.

00:09:22.334 --> 00:09:25.400
The judge forcing
Trump's lawyer, Chris Kise,

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:29.133
to talk to the former president.

00:09:29.133 --> 00:09:31.133
The former president,
we're reading here,

00:09:31.133 --> 00:09:34.033
apparently waved his arms
at any suggestion

00:09:34.033 --> 00:09:36.234
of taking a 10 minute break.

00:09:36.234 --> 00:09:38.734
He is sitting back in his chair,
we're told,

00:09:38.734 --> 00:09:43.467
just pursing his lips in that
sort of classic Trump smile.

00:09:43.467 --> 00:09:45.367
Trump's lawyer is assuring
the judge

00:09:45.367 --> 00:09:48.567
that their client
"understands the rules."

00:09:48.567 --> 00:09:50.367
The judge shot back and said,

00:09:50.367 --> 00:09:52.834
"Well, he doesn't
abide by them."

00:09:52.834 --> 00:09:55.267
Now, apparently they're back
into questioning.

00:09:55.267 --> 00:09:56.934
-This is kind of
a frustrating way

00:09:56.934 --> 00:09:58.434
to hear what's
going on in court.

00:09:58.434 --> 00:10:02.701
It's like listening
to hockey on NPR.

00:10:02.701 --> 00:10:04.501
Like, you know,
the action is crazy,

00:10:04.501 --> 00:10:06.767
but it's so confusing
to listen to.

00:10:06.767 --> 00:10:09.834
Let's see, we're getting more
reporting from the courthouse.

00:10:09.834 --> 00:10:13.200
Yes, Mr. Trump waved
his hands and pursed his lips.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.801
Then he moved them in and out

00:10:14.801 --> 00:10:17.767
like he was playing
an invisible accordion.

00:10:17.767 --> 00:10:20.334
Then he began drawing
little boxes with his fingers

00:10:20.334 --> 00:10:23.300
and pointing to his head,
saying, "I understand the rules.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.434
I have them all up here
in my big brain."

00:10:25.434 --> 00:10:26.901
Then the judge shot back,

00:10:26.901 --> 00:10:29.100
"You're not acting
like you know the rules."

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:32.367
Then Trump said, "Am, too."
And the judge said, "Am not."

00:10:32.367 --> 00:10:35.767
Then Trump said "Am, too."
Then the judge said, "Am not."

00:10:35.767 --> 00:10:39.067
Then Trump said, "It smells
like updog in here."

00:10:39.067 --> 00:10:42.200
Then the judge said,
"I'm not falling for that."

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.367
Then Trump said,
"I don't know, dog.

00:10:44.367 --> 00:10:46.100
What's up with you?"

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:49.200
Then the judge said, "You can't
just act like I fell for it.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.767
Loser says what?"
Then Trump said, "What?"

00:10:51.767 --> 00:10:53.400
Then the judge said,
"You said what.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.467
That means you're a loser."

00:10:55.467 --> 00:10:58.567
Then Trump got angry
and screamed, "This is warfare!

00:10:58.567 --> 00:11:02.534
No, wait. It's lawfare.
No wait. It's law unfair."

00:11:02.534 --> 00:11:05.501
Then he got up and tried
to storm out of the courtroom,

00:11:05.501 --> 00:11:07.601
but his tie got stuck
in the door

00:11:07.601 --> 00:11:09.567
and he fell backwards
and split his pants

00:11:09.567 --> 00:11:13.968
and threw up on himself,
and the judge called a recess.

00:11:13.968 --> 00:11:15.734
And Trump said,
"The judge [bleep] in my pants."

00:11:15.734 --> 00:11:17.901
And the judge said,
"No, I didn't."

00:11:17.901 --> 00:11:20.133
Then Trump said, "Then how
did [bleep] get in my pants?"

00:11:20.133 --> 00:11:23.300
Then the judge said,
"Maybe it was updog."

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:25.400
Then Trump said,
"What's updog?"

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:27.601
Then the judge said, "I don't
know. what's up with you?"

00:11:27.601 --> 00:11:29.534
And the entire courtroom
laughed.

00:11:29.534 --> 00:11:32.801
[ Laughter ]

00:11:32.801 --> 00:11:34.434
Back to you, Kate.

00:11:34.434 --> 00:11:37.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:37.834 --> 00:11:39.367
Although I guess
the judge's warning

00:11:39.367 --> 00:11:40.934
did start to sink in with Trump
at some point

00:11:40.934 --> 00:11:43.434
because as he left the courtroom
for a morning break,

00:11:43.434 --> 00:11:45.000
reporters tried
to ask him a question

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.601
and he just made a lip seal
gesture as he walked away.

00:11:49.901 --> 00:11:52.934
-Mr. Trump,
has it going in there?

00:11:52.934 --> 00:11:55.167
[ Laughter ]

00:11:57.801 --> 00:11:59.801
-He could have said no comment
like a grown up,

00:11:59.801 --> 00:12:01.701
but of course he did
a goofy gesture

00:12:01.701 --> 00:12:05.734
like an eighth-grade girl
who knows about your crush.

00:12:05.734 --> 00:12:07.634
The only time he's made
that gesture in his life

00:12:07.634 --> 00:12:09.767
was when his kids asked him
to read a bedtime story.

00:12:09.767 --> 00:12:13.634
"Sorry, boys.
I'm under a gag order."

00:12:13.634 --> 00:12:16.701
The 2024 presidential election
is still a year away,

00:12:16.701 --> 00:12:18.501
and a lot can happen,
but no one should doubt

00:12:18.501 --> 00:12:21.100
that as of this moment,
Trump could very well win,

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:22.834
which would give him the power
to pardon himself,

00:12:22.834 --> 00:12:24.167
essentially
erase his indictments,

00:12:24.167 --> 00:12:25.834
and officially declare himself
above the law.

00:12:25.834 --> 00:12:27.634
Again,
as we've seen before,

00:12:27.634 --> 00:12:31.300
a lot can change and will change
between now and next November.

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:32.801
So when it comes
to the election,

00:12:32.801 --> 00:12:35.534
all we can do for now is just
stay calm while we...

00:12:35.534 --> 00:12:36.834
-Wait for it.

00:12:36.834 --> 00:12:40.133
[ Laughter ]

00:12:40.133 --> 00:12:41.567
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:41.567 --> 00:12:43.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:45.033 --> 00:12:46.901
Hey, everybody. Thanks for
watching "A Closer Look."

00:12:46.901 --> 00:12:48.667
And as a reminder,
my brother Josh

00:12:48.667 --> 00:12:52.067
and I have started a new podcast
called "Family Trips"

00:12:52.067 --> 00:12:54.367
with the Meyers Brothers.
We hope you listen.

00:12:54.367 --> 00:12:56.133
We hope you like it,
and see you soon.

